WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:04.029
Floods can carry cholera into wells and water tanks.

2
00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:08.620
Cholera spreads through dirty water and food, and it can kill within hours.

3
00:00:08.669 --> 00:00:11.740
But it can be prevented, and it can be treated.

4
00:00:11.989 --> 00:00:13.860
Here is how to protect your family.

5
00:00:14.722 --> 00:00:18.151
The cholera germ lives in the faeces of infected people.

6
00:00:18.162 --> 00:00:22.602
When floodwater or overflowing latrines reach wells, tanks and food,

7
00:00:22.602 --> 00:00:23.871
the germ gets in.

8
00:00:24.041 --> 00:00:28.752
Most people who swallow it have mild illness or none, but they can still spread it.

9
00:00:28.842 --> 00:00:33.192
Some become very sick, with sudden, watery diarrhoea and vomiting.

10
00:00:34.078 --> 00:00:36.507
First, make drinking water safe.

11
00:00:36.558 --> 00:00:39.708
Bring the water to a rolling boil, with big bubbles,

12
00:00:39.758 --> 00:00:41.398
then let it cool with the lid on.

13
00:00:41.398 --> 00:00:46.108
If you cannot boil it, use water treatment tablets exactly as the packet says.

14
00:00:46.157 --> 00:00:50.988
Use safe water for drinking, cooking, brushing teeth and making baby food.

15
00:00:51.898 --> 00:00:54.617
Keep safe water in a clean container with a lid.

16
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:57.018
Pour it out, or use a tap.

17
00:00:57.018 --> 00:01:00.888
Never dip your hands, or a dirty cup, into stored water.

18
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:05.139
Second, wash your hands with soap and clean water.

19
00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.470
Wet your hands and rub in soap.

20
00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:12.979
Scrub every part: palms, backs, between the fingers and under the nails.

21
00:01:13.149 --> 00:01:15.660
Rinse, and let them dry in the air.

22
00:01:15.749 --> 00:01:19.630
Do it after the toilet, after cleaning a child, before cooking,

23
00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:21.980
and before eating or feeding a child.

24
00:01:22.858 --> 00:01:25.688
Third, keep faeces away from water.

25
00:01:25.697 --> 00:01:30.728
Always use a latrine, never open ground, and keep latrines far from wells.

26
00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:35.288
Put children's faeces in the latrine too, and wash your hands afterwards.

27
00:01:36.166 --> 00:01:38.646
Fourth, make food safe.

28
00:01:38.646 --> 00:01:41.356
Cook food well and eat it while it is hot.

29
00:01:41.486 --> 00:01:45.475
Wash fruit with safe water and peel it, and keep food covered.

30
00:01:46.378 --> 00:01:49.418
If someone has watery diarrhoea, act fast.

31
00:01:49.418 --> 00:01:53.768
Start oral rehydration solution, ORS, straight away.

32
00:01:53.778 --> 00:01:57.537
Mix one packet with safe water exactly as the packet says,

33
00:01:57.537 --> 00:01:59.687
and give small sips often.

34
00:01:59.788 --> 00:02:03.828
Go to a health facility quickly, especially if the person is very weak,

35
00:02:03.828 --> 00:02:06.418
cannot drink, or is a young child.

36
00:02:06.708 --> 00:02:09.337
Most people recover with quick ORS.

37
00:02:10.246 --> 00:02:14.165
Where health workers offer the oral cholera vaccine, take it,

38
00:02:14.165 --> 00:02:17.156
and keep boiling water and washing hands.

39
00:02:17.286 --> 00:02:21.076
Safe water, clean hands, quick ORS.

40
00:02:21.286 --> 00:02:22.955
Share this with your family.
